# Build artefacts. A plugin here ships as SOURCE and is compiled on the machine
# that installs it, so neither of these belongs in the repository.
#
# `build/` is where the engine drops the compiled library, its `stamp.txt` and
# the `.reload/` shadow copies it swaps between on a hot reload. `target/` is
# cargo's. Across the plugins in this repository they came to 1.7 GB against
# 2.2 MB of actual source.
build/
target/

# The receipt the marketplace installer writes beside an installed plugin. It
# records THAT machine's copy — an asset id, the slug and version it was
# installed at — so it belongs to an install and not to source. Committed, it
# hands every clone a pointer to one person's assets, and goes stale the moment
# a new version is published.
plugin.toml
